{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Theoretically, scores on the math sections of the ACT and SAT college entrance examinations are normally distributed. For the ACT, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f08c7de1f8951cecc907c2f06da3ec0b250585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu = 18, \\sigma = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" /> and for the SAT, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/5/c35ff5b75be4f0b5468c475db0350a88a5bbdc4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu = 500, \\sigma = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"17\" />. All scores on the ACT are recorded as whole numbers and all scores on the SAT are recorded as multiples of 10. If a student scores a 27 on the math section of the ACT, what would the corresponding score be on the SAT using equivalent z-scores?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be86dfc9bf696ba93a3feaaa52428648e3af202a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 450 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 570 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 590 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 650 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 710$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"442\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/a/dda226195338d04ed24f72b318453210226d0f4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27 - \\mu = 27 - 18 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"169\" height=\"17\" /> for the ACT, so this score would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08dd1b5545e0c6e043aedd2ea918742618db1b6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{\\sigma} = \\frac{9}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"54\" height=\"38\" /> standard deviations above the mean, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfdbd19877c13d1755e01b54ba640f512c883a34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> standard deviations above the mean.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfdbd19877c13d1755e01b54ba640f512c883a34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> standard deviations above the mean is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f07798800b68cc054b07c68d43930daefc71491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma \\times \\frac{3}{2} = 100 \\times \\frac{3}{2} = 150$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"186\" height=\"38\" /> above the mean for the SAT, so the equivalent score would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/6/f6617b58079b66103dbda23ef58ab70e8abf3bf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500 + 150 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 650}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"177\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest\">2025 TMTA Algebra II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Problems/Problem 5\"